WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:08.828
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:15.820
Unit eight: Listening: Announcements. Today you will understand campus announcements and answer inference questions.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.935
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.144
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:25.031
Announcement.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.597
Announcement means a spoken public message.

8
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.788
Listen to the announcement.

9
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.908
Your turn. Say: Announcement.

10
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:37.710
Announcement.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.254
Cancel.

12
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.668
Cancel means to stop an event from happening.

13
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:44.760
The class is cancelled.

14
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.631
Your turn. Say: Cancel.

15
00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.352
Cancel.

16
00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:53.013
Reschedule.

17
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:56.794
Reschedule means to change the time of an event.

18
00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:58.918
The lecture is rescheduled.

19
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:02.065
Your turn. Say: Reschedule.

20
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.948
Reschedule.

21
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:07.673
Venue.

22
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:10.613
Venue means the place of an event.

23
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:12.612
The venue has changed.

24
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.544
Your turn. Say: Venue.

25
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.250
Venue.

26
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:20.913
Reminder.

27
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:24.624
Reminder means a message to help you remember.

28
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.485
This is a reminder.

29
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:29.736
Your turn. Say: Reminder.

30
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.624
Reminder.

31
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:35.350
Eligible.

32
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.628
Eligible means allowed to take part.

33
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:41.727
Only first-year students are eligible.

34
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:44.574
Your turn. Say: Eligible.

35
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:48.458
Eligible.

36
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:50.171
Attend.

37
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:53.717
Attend means to be present at an event.

38
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:55.701
Please attend the meeting.

39
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:59.155
Your turn. Say: Attend.

40
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.850
Attend.

41
00:02:03.617 --> 00:02:04.618
Inference.

42
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:08.708
Inference means an idea you understand from clues.

43
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:10.759
Make an inference.

44
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.979
Your turn. Say: Inference.

45
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:17.916
Inference.

46
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.676
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:26.306
Visal, what is in a campus announcement?

48
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:36.115
The speaker gives information such as a change of time, a new venue or an upcoming event, and then tells listeners what to do.

49
00:02:37.217 --> 00:02:39.007
What are the key points to catch?

50
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:49.805
Listen for what is happening, when and where it will happen, who is affected, and what action is needed. Numbers and times need careful attention.

51
00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:52.452
What do the questions ask?

52
00:02:53.550 --> 00:03:05.386
They ask for details, the purpose of the announcement and inferences, such as why the event is moving. Answer only with information the speaker gives or clearly suggests.

53
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:08.115
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.213
Grammar focus: Strategy: what, when, where, who, action.

55
00:03:13.513 --> 00:03:14.758
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:18.204
The lecture has been moved to Hall B at three o'clock.

57
00:03:19.117 --> 00:03:22.347
Only first-year students are eligible to join the trip.

58
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:29.911
Take short notes on what, when, where and who, and listen for the action required. For inference, use the clues the speaker gives.

59
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.208
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore times and numbers.

60
00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.886
Say: I note times and numbers.

61
00:03:39.186 --> 00:03:40.373
Note numbers.

62
00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.761
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.079
A Change of Plan.

64
00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:49.597
A speaker announces that tomorrow's lecture is rescheduled.

65
00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.470
It will now take place in Hall B at three o'clock.

66
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.977
The reason is that the usual room is being repaired.

67
00:03:57.967 --> 00:04:00.744
Students are reminded to bring their ID cards.

68
00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:05.858
Only first-year students are eligible for the library tour afterwards.

69
00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:10.864
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.368
The lecture is now in blank.

71
00:04:13.668 --> 00:04:17.159
A, Room 1. B, the library. C, Hall B.

72
00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.595
The answer is C: Hall B.

73
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.274
Why was the room changed?

74
00:04:25.574 --> 00:04:30.550
A, it is being repaired. B, it is too big. C, it is closed for a party.

75
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.738
The answer is A: it is being repaired.

76
00:04:37.883 --> 00:04:39.535
Students should bring blank.

77
00:04:39.835 --> 00:04:43.929
A, money only. B, ID cards. C, tickets.

78
00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:50.070
The answer is B: ID cards.

79
00:04:51.217 --> 00:04:52.763
Rescheduled means blank.

80
00:04:53.063 --> 00:04:57.355
A, cancelled. B, finished. C, changed the time.

81
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.062
The answer is C: changed the time.

82
00:05:04.217 --> 00:05:06.414
Who is eligible for the library tour?

83
00:05:06.714 --> 00:05:11.249
A, first-year students. B, all staff. C, no one.

84
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.566
The answer is A: first-year students.

85
00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:21.918
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:24.458
How do you follow an announcement?

87
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.110
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:47.202
I listen for what is happening, when and where it will take place, and who is affected. I write short notes with numbers and times. Then I listen for the action that listeners must take.

89
00:05:47.502 --> 00:05:49.165
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:55.129
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: what, when, where, who, action.

91
00:05:55.429 --> 00:05:59.985
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:00.285 --> 00:06:02.670
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.901
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

